bounty-item-soviet-pin = soviet pin
bounty-description-soviet-pin-collector = A private collector of old Soviet pins is preparing a large themed event and desperately needs ten more pieces. They insist this is absolutely not related to any mutiny plans.
bounty-item-soviet-damaged-id-card = damaged soviet ID card
bounty-description-soviet-damaged-id-cards-collector = An expedition archivist is building a collection of damaged Soviet ID cards for a frontier history exhibition and needs any six specimens.
bounty-item-soviet-damaged-officer-id-card = damaged soviet officer ID card
bounty-description-soviet-damaged-officer-id-cards-collector = A collector of military relics is ready to buy three damaged Soviet junior officer ID cards for a private exhibit.

bounty-item-sunrise-vaccine = vaccine
bounty-description-sunrise-vaccine = CentCom's medical department is restocking vaccines for nearby stations in the sector. A vaccine against any strain will do.
bounty-item-sunrise-serum = serum
bounty-description-sunrise-serum = A sector hospital urgently needs serum from the blood of recovered patients. The strain does not matter: it will be studied and used as a reference.
bounty-item-sunrise-strain-sample = strain sample
bounty-description-sunrise-strain-samples = A CentCom research center is collecting strains found on stations. Any vial with a sample will do, but not empty blanks.
bounty-item-sunrise-designed-strain = designed strain
bounty-description-sunrise-designed-strain = A NanoTrasen lab wants to study a strain designed under your virology microscope. Send the original microscope vial; database copies are not accepted.
